    "result": "**Result:** The electronics dataset is `items_g2` / `fdbk_g2` (15,975 of its 20,000 items sit in electronics `main_cat`s, vs. office-heavy g1 and instrument-heavy g3). Reviews join via `fdbk_g2.ref_id = items_g2.ref_id` (100% coverage; the alternative `item_id` column matches only 64%), and `prc` is USD cents (`prc = prc_usd × 100` exactly), so the $40 list-price cap is `prc_usd <= 40`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"10.22\",\n  \"sql\": \"SELECT ROUND(100.0 * SUM(f.rtg = 1) / COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_1star FROM fdbk_g2 f JOIN items_g2 i ON i.ref_id = f.ref_id WHERE LENGTH(f.body) > 500 AND i.prc_usd <= 40\"\n}\n```\n\n222 of the 2,172 qualifying electronics reviews are 1-star → **10.22%**.\n\nReusable findings (group→category mapping, join-key choice, cents-vs-USD price units) were written to `memory/environment.md` with evidence and inference/verification labels, and indexed in `memory/MEMORY.md`; the computed percentage is deliberately excluded from those notes.",
